<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Receipt OCR (SPEC.md §5.3, ADR-0021).

  CAMERA is the second permission this app has ever asked for by choice, and
  unlike RECEIVE_SMS it is not flavour-restricted: §5.3's capture path is in
  both flavours, because OCR is one of the two ingest sources playSafe ships.
  So it lives in src/main and merges into both, and `restrictedPermissionCheck`
  pins it here rather than treating its presence as a surprise.

  **Runtime, and genuinely optional.** `uses-feature required="false"` is the
  load-bearing half: a device with no camera must still install and still be
  able to import a receipt from the gallery or a PDF via SAF, which §5.3 lists
  as first-class inputs alongside capture. Declaring the feature as required
  would silently remove the app from those devices' store listings and, for a
  sideload, offer no signal at all.

  No INTERNET here. ML Kit merges it from `transport-backend-cct` and that is
  recorded in :app's EXPECTED_MERGED_PERMISSIONS with its reason; it is
  deliberately not restated in a source manifest, because writing it here would
  read as this module asking for the network, which it does not.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA" />

    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.camera"
        android:required="false" />

</manifest>
